const faqs = [
  { q: "Why is my flight-type dishwasher conveyor belt not moving?", a: "A flight-type dishwasher conveyor belt that won't advance usually traces to one of three causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across Hobart FT2000 / FT-900 / FT-1000 / FT-1500 commercial flight-type installations. (1) Conveyor drive motor failure year 8-12 — motor bearing wear or brush failure means belt doesn't advance regardless of controller signal. $550-$950 motor replacement, 90-120 minutes. (2) Belt drive sprocket wear year 10-12 — sprocket teeth wear leads to belt slippage or uneven advance. $380-$580 sprocket replacement. (3) Belt tension or alignment drift — belt has stretched past adjustment range, or alignment has shifted to point of binding. $180-$340 belt adjustment service or $480-$820 belt replacement. Plus operator-side issues: belt jammed with debris (clears at diagnostic visit), end-of-belt safety switch tripped. Our techs verify drive motor amp draw + sprocket visual + belt tension + safety switch continuity on every flight-type belt-not-moving call." },
  { q: "What's the difference between flight-type and rack-conveyor dishwashers?", a: "Two distinct continuous-conveyor commercial dishwasher architectures with different operational profiles. Flight-type (Hobart FT2000 / FT-900 / FT-1000 / FT-1500) uses a continuous belt that carries dishes / trays through wash + rinse zones without racks — dishes placed directly on the belt, belt advances continuously. Throughput 1,000+ pieces per hour for institutional cafeteria operations. Common installations: LAUSD school nutrition, hospital cafeteria, university dining halls, stadium concessions. Rack-conveyor (Hobart CL44eN / CRS, Jackson AJ + AJX / RackStar, Champion 86) uses discrete dish racks moving on continuous conveyor mechanism — dishes loaded into racks, racks advance through wash zones. Throughput 200-400 racks per hour for restaurant + smaller cafeteria operations. Different parts (belt vs sprocket-driven rack mechanism), different service intervals, different operator workflow. See sister page <a href=\"/commercial/dishwasher-repair/rack-conveyor-dishwasher-repair/\">rack conveyor dishwasher repair</a>." },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between flight type and rack conveyor?",
    a: "Rack conveyor moves racks of dishes through wash zones, throughput 200 to 400 racks per hour, restaurant scale. Flight type uses a continuous flight of pegs (no racks) that carries individual plates and trays through pre-wash, wash, rinse, and final-rinse zones, throughput 1,000+ pieces per hour, hospital and university scale. Different drive system, different repair playbook."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you service Hobart FT-900, FT-1000, and FT-1500?",
    a: "Yes. The Hobart FT line dominates institutional installs in LA hospitals and universities. We carry common conveyor motors, scrap collector parts, multi-zone door switches, and tank heater elements for these models. FT-900 (smaller institutional), FT-1000 (mid), FT-1500 (large hospital and university scale)."
  },
  {
    q: "My flight type's pre-rinse spray nozzles are clogged. What's the fix?",
    a: "Hard-water mineral scale buildup on spray nozzles is the most common pre-rinse issue. Solution: deep descale of pre-rinse manifold and nozzles. We use food-safe descaler, run a cleaning cycle, verify spray pattern, document. $360 to $580 typical. If nozzle ports are heavily corroded past cleaning, replacement is required."
  },
  {
    q: "Tank heater is steam-injected. Do you do steam line work?",
    a: "We do the dishwasher-side steam injection (steam control valve, steam coil cleaning, condensate trap servicing). We don't do upstream steam supply line work, that's a steam plumbing trade. If your steam supply pressure is off, we identify it and refer to a steam contractor."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the typical service call cost on a Hobart FT?",
    a: "$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair. Most flight type repairs run $980 to $2,400 all-in due to scale and complexity. Conveyor motor, tank heater, multi-zone door switch chain, scrap collector. We provide HACCP temperature documentation post-repair for institutional records."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty?",
    a: "90 days SDAR labor warranty on every repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

